The collision happens inside the compiled serializer when extras are merged after declared fields. I’m adding a narrowly scoped `model_dump` guard: only when an extra key matches the actual output key of a declared field, serialize a shallow copy with that colliding extra removed. This preserves aliases, field serializers, context, and all existing dump options.
